        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "I have a question about applying the Focused Apparatus ability from Elemental Manipulator against multiple targets.  The definition states \"Hinder using [power].  Attack using your Min die.  If you are in the Red zone, you may apply the penalty to any number of nearby targets.\"  I could read this two different ways when using the ability in the Red zone:  \n1) A player could Hinder and Attack any number of nearby targets.  \n2) A player would only get the Attack function against one target, while applying the Hinder against numerous targets.  \nMy reasoning would be that the definition says to \"apply the penalty.\"  Are both Hinder and Attack results both considered penalties?  Or are Hinder results penalties and Attack results damages and therefore not spread out over multiple targets.  It might depend on how carefully one parses the language.  Any thoughts of exactly what is intended?",
