        "id": 261829,
        "name": "Chief Lackey Rich",
        "username": "Chief_Lackey_Rich",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2024-12-19T13:23:13.578Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Right, although it’s also worth noting that you can Hinder one (or many, in Red) target with your Mid while Attacking any one target you like with your Min, not just one you Hindered.</p>\n<p>There are situations where you might not want to Hinder and Attack the same target, and this ability doesn’t force you to.  Examples include wanting to avoid triggering a target’s reaction to taking damage or knowing that even your Min damage should finish a target so your penalty is better put somewhere else.  Adds a little bit of extra versatility, even if you may not need it all that often.</p>\n<p>If your team’s light on multi-target Hinders (and they often are, those are pretty rare) this can be a good ability to bank a few bonuses for when you hit Red one way or another.  Dropping a -3 or -4 penalty across most or all of the opposition can be game changing, although the miniscule damage output on one target isn’t likely to matter.  Most EE archetypes use some kind of damage immunity/inversion trick and focus on the self-harming Green Attack abilities, but this one (and the Defend/Boost Green) do open up other builds - not to mention being the only Hinder the archetype provides.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2024-12-19T13:31:50.456Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
