        "username": "Chief_Lackey_Rich",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2024-12-19T22:53:55.428Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"fjur\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"31235\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/48/4849_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> fjur:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And even with the basic version of the ability without the extra Red zone effect, you could use it to Hinder one target while Attacking another, as otherwise the ability would tell you to Attack the <em>same</em> target.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Right.  Compare and contrast with the Tech Upgrade power source’s Organi-Hack ability, which reads “Attack a target with (power).  Hinder that target with your Min die.”  If the default Mid die damage from that Attack KOs the target, the Min die penalty is going to waste.</p>",
